  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1051 PM CDT Tue Jun 30 2026\n\nNot much has changed for the longer term portion of the forecast,\nwith hot and dry and not as breezy prevailing through the 4th of\nJuly. As noted the last few days, the upper level ridge is still\nforecasted to weaken across the southeast US, allowing a little\nbit of a weak shear axis and then upper level low to develop\nacross Texas. Scattered showers and storms will be possible Sunday\ninto Monday. Not expecting widespread rainfall but the low to\nmedium chances (20-40) are higher chances than anything much of  \nWest Central Texas has seen in some weeks.",
